    "level": "b1",
    "unit": 36,
    "title": "Linking Words (although/despite/however)",
    "title_ko": "대조 접속사 (although/despite/however)",
    "focus_axis": "grammar"
  },
  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "'Although' + clause connects two contrasting ideas in one sentence: 'Although it was raining, we went out.' 'Despite' + noun/-ing does the same: 'Despite the rain, we went out.' 'However' starts a new sentence: 'It was raining. However, we went out.'",
    "explanation_ko": "'although' + 절은 한 문장 안에서 대조되는 두 생각을 연결합니다: 'Although it was raining, we went out.' 'despite' + 명사/-ing도 같은 역할을 합니다: 'Despite the rain, we went out.' 'however'는 새 문장을 시작합니다: 'It was raining. However, we went out.'",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "Although I was tired, I finished the work.",
        "ko": "피곤했지만 저는 일을 끝냈어요."
      },
      {
        "en": "Despite the traffic, we arrived on time.",
        "ko": "교통 체증에도 불구하고 우리는 제시간에 도착했어요."
      },
      {
        "en": "The plan was risky. However, it worked.",
        "ko": "그 계획은 위험했어요. 하지만 성공했어요."
      }
    ]
  },
